<title>ITALY: Interbanca privilege shares suspended.</title>
<headline>Interbanca privilege shares suspended.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's stock market regulator Consob said privilege shares in Interbanca had been suspended pending an announcement on the company's future later on Thursday.</p>
<p>A Consob statement said the suspension was effective from 1205 GMT. Interbanca privilege shares closed at 37,500 lire on February 5.</p>
<p>Banca di Roma was expected to announce later on Thursday that it was selling Interbanca to Banca Antoniana Veneta. The two companies have called a news conference in Rome for 1430 GMT.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
